A||||5||pontiacs4me||differences between different year fascias?||||1||
Z||000000||pontiacs4me||02-27-2001||07:46 PM||||I was wondering if there is a difference between different year gt/se rear fascias?  If there is does anybody have a link to a site with pics of the different styles?  How about wings.  I look at alot of pics of fieros with wings and some seem to look like they sit much higher than others.  Does anybody know the differences in these (if any).  Thanks.||||reg||1
Z||000001||rockcrawl||02-27-2001||08:29 PM||||As far as I know there are 6 different types of rear fascias. <BR>(1)the early 4cyl coupe style used on all 4cyl coupes from 84-86 and the 84-85 4cyl SE. <BR>(2)the early V6 coupe style used on all V6 coupes from 85-86 and the 85 V6 SE. <BR>(3)the early aero style used on the 84 Indy, 85 GT, and 86-87 SE. <BR>(4)the late coupe style used on the 87-88 4cyl coupe <BR>(5)the 88 Formula style. <BR>(6)the late aero style used on the 86-88 GT. <P>The coupe fascias had one exhaust opening or two depending on wether it was a 4cyl or V6, but that is the only difference. The aero fascias all have dual exhaust even the 86-87 4cyl SE's.<P>All of the factory spoilers were the same, but higher stanchions are available from the aftermarket.<P>Someone please correct me if I made any errors or left anything out.<P>------------------<BR>Jon Lagler<BR>'87 GT<BR>4.9 liter V8 Testarossa Spyder (under construction)<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/rockcrawlsig.jpg">  <p>[This message has been edited by rockcrawl (edited 02-27-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||Galen||02-27-2001||09:20 PM||||the 88 formula and 88 coupe fascia's are the same, both have the dual cutouts ..  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000003||Raydar||02-27-2001||11:13 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by rockcrawl:<BR><B>All of the factory spoilers were the same, but higher stanchions are available from the aftermarket.<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>This info wasn't really asked for, but...<P>All of the wings ARE the same, but the ones mounted on the fastback GTs have the mounting studs in different holes than the notchbacks. Not a big deal, though. The studs will unscrew and can be put in the alternate holes with little problem.<BR><P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<P>88 T-top Formula<BR>88 soon-to-be-V6 coupe||||reg||1
Z||000004||William||02-28-2001||12:32 AM||||Correction...The 85 SE V-6 used the early coupe rear facia  :-)||||reg||1
Z||000005||rockcrawl||02-28-2001||08:20 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>the 88 formula and 88 coupe fascia's are the same, both have the dual cutouts<HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>OK, so #4 and #5 are the same thing. Thanks.<P> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>The 85 SE V-6 used the early coupe rear facia<HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>#1 and #2 on my list are identical except for the # of exhaust openings. I have the 85 SE V6 in category #2 meaning that it has a coupe style fascia with two exhaust outlets. Are you saying the 85 SE had a single exhaust, or that it had a dual exhaust with only a cutout for the exhaust on the left side? I'm not sure about this one.||||reg||1
